<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mufarraj ibn Sallam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mufarraj ibn Sallam was the second ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, in power in the 850s. He extended Muslim conquests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, built a congregational mosque in Bari, and sought formal recognition as emir from the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>. He was murdered by his own troops around 857 and succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sawdan">Sawdan</a>.</p></div>
